Yeah.

775
00:32:54.540 --> 00:32:56.820
Well, you're so great in this scene.

776
00:32:57.020 --> 00:33:02.800
I really would love someone to write a series for you that is like this character.

777
00:33:03.120 --> 00:33:08.100
The one sipping on the big gulp at her wits end?

778
00:33:08.560 --> 00:33:09.340
Kind of.

779
00:33:09.460 --> 00:33:09.700
Yeah.

780
00:33:09.960 --> 00:33:11.600
You're really great at it.

781
00:33:11.720 --> 00:33:12.220
Thanks.

782
00:33:12.420 --> 00:33:13.800
I think this could be a series.

783
00:33:14.180 --> 00:33:16.820
This character could have a journey.

784
00:33:16.820 --> 00:33:20.500
And I'd like to follow that thread with you in the lead.

785
00:33:20.800 --> 00:33:22.740
Well, it would certainly be a fun role.

786
00:33:23.040 --> 00:33:23.860
I agree.

787
00:33:23.860 --> 00:33:26.660
And I'd never have to worry about doing the back of my hair ever.

788
00:33:26.900 --> 00:33:27.640
Oh, no, no, no, no.

789
00:33:27.840 --> 00:33:29.660
That character does not do the back of her hair.

790
00:33:31.000 --> 00:33:33.940
She aggressively does not do the back of her hair.

791
00:33:34.160 --> 00:33:36.900
And the cowlick that I have would just be...

792
00:33:36.900 --> 00:33:37.440
It just works.

793
00:33:37.560 --> 00:33:40.040
It would just be an accent on the perfect hairdo.

794
00:33:40.240 --> 00:33:40.580
Exactly.

795
00:33:40.900 --> 00:33:42.620
I do want to point out one thing in the script.

796
00:33:42.800 --> 00:33:50.460
At the end of the scene between Angela and Andy, when Angela walks away would be the moment that Andy clocks David Wallace's car.

797
00:33:50.460 --> 00:33:51.160
Uh-huh.

798
00:33:51.340 --> 00:33:53.280
And makes the decision to poop on it.

799
00:33:53.620 --> 00:33:54.260
I see.

800
00:33:54.260 --> 00:34:00.420
And so then when he walks into the bullpen with his guitar and says, no turning back, it's because he's already pooped on the car.

801
00:34:00.840 --> 00:34:01.000
Yeah.

802
00:34:01.480 --> 00:34:01.900
Okay.

803
00:34:01.900 --> 00:34:14.640
Well, this next scene, I mean, if you wanted to make a lady sob at her desk at 2.30 in the afternoon on a Tuesday, congratulations, mission accomplished.

804
00:34:15.460 --> 00:34:19.440
I watched this, and I wasn't the same for the rest of the day.

805
00:34:19.760 --> 00:34:22.560
This is when Andy came in with his guitar, Lorelai.

806
00:34:22.720 --> 00:34:23.080
Mm-hmm.

807
00:34:23.240 --> 00:34:25.000
He wants to sing his goodbye.

808
00:34:25.560 --> 00:34:27.980
He's a performer, and that's how he wants to say goodbye.

809
00:34:27.980 --> 00:34:37.340
Yeah, there was a fan question from Alexandra in Tasmania, Australia, who said, I love the scene where Andy sings I Will Remember You by Sarah McLachlan,

810
00:34:37.420 --> 00:34:45.420
and I think it's such a great choice for Andy to sing it in a normal singing voice and not his usual kind of a cappella theatrical singing voice.

811
00:34:45.720 --> 00:34:49.120
Was that scripted, or did Ed Helms choose to sing that way?

812
00:34:49.480 --> 00:34:51.500
Well, Alexandra, it was scripted.

813
00:34:51.800 --> 00:34:56.800
It was scripted that the song is good and that everyone in the office is impressed.

814
00:34:56.800 --> 00:34:57.420
Mm-hmm.

815
00:34:57.960 --> 00:35:13.720
Steve Burgess said that that song cost $25,000 for us to be able to do, and I think that when I watched this scene, it brought back so many deep personal memories from shooting it,

816
00:35:13.720 --> 00:35:15.580
and I really was not the same the rest of the day.

817
00:35:15.740 --> 00:35:18.640
And then I dreamt about the show that night.

818
00:35:18.900 --> 00:35:19.540
I dreamt.

819
00:35:19.800 --> 00:35:21.180
Does this ever happen to you?

820
00:35:21.320 --> 00:35:25.460
I have dreams where we're back on set, and we're making more episodes.

821
00:35:25.460 --> 00:35:27.480
It's like we're making season 10.

822
00:35:27.760 --> 00:35:27.900
Yeah.

823
00:35:28.140 --> 00:35:34.380
Yeah, I've had that similar dream that I am walking from hair and makeup to get miked.

824
00:35:34.600 --> 00:35:34.880
Yeah.

825
00:35:35.180 --> 00:35:45.160
To go onto stage, and the stage is right there, and I'm looking at our desks, and I'm about to walk into the bullpen, and I'm getting miked, and it's so real.

826
00:35:45.380 --> 00:35:45.960
So real.

827
00:35:46.140 --> 00:35:49.980
Watching this for this rewatch triggered that, and I ended up having a dream.

828
00:35:49.980 --> 00:35:53.740
Also in my dream, we all pick up right where we left off.

829
00:35:54.040 --> 00:35:54.620
Yes, exactly.

830
00:35:54.840 --> 00:35:57.540
Like no one has to get reacquainted with their character.

831
00:35:57.540 --> 00:35:59.360
We're instantly those people again.

832
00:35:59.700 --> 00:35:59.940
Yeah.

833
00:36:00.080 --> 00:36:03.680
It's not like those anxiety dreams where like, oh, no, I don't know my lines.

834
00:36:03.680 --> 00:36:05.620
It's always like this pleasurable.

835
00:36:05.760 --> 00:36:07.080
I'm getting emotional thinking about it.

836
00:36:07.080 --> 00:36:09.980
But I'm going to move to a fan question from Maddie R.

837
00:36:10.160 --> 00:36:11.540
in Kansas City who said,

838
00:36:11.680 --> 00:36:16.080
When Andy sings to the office, we see lots of emotional reactions from the staff.

839
00:36:16.220 --> 00:36:21.700
Were any of the emotions we see real reactions from the cast being sad about the show ending?

840
00:36:22.200 --> 00:36:28.360
Well, Maddie, we shot this at the end of the day on Friday.

841
00:36:28.360 --> 00:36:36.080
So the end of the day, at the end of the week, it was the last group scene we shot for this episode, and it was deeply emotional.

842
00:36:36.760 --> 00:36:38.260
It was very emotional.

843
00:36:39.220 --> 00:36:44.860
You know, we just all knew that there was just a few more weeks left at this point.

844
00:36:45.720 --> 00:36:48.000
And Andy was really saying goodbye.

845
00:36:48.640 --> 00:36:50.520
This character is saying goodbye.

846
00:36:51.300 --> 00:36:55.200
And right before we did the scene, there were two camera setups.

847
00:36:55.200 --> 00:37:04.420
There was a master shot to get everyone, and then there was going to be a close-up of me and Rain as Dwight and Angela have their exchange.

848
00:37:06.220 --> 00:37:10.640
And Jeff came up to me and said, Save it for your close-up.

849
00:37:11.040 --> 00:37:16.400
So feel the emotion, but really let it come through on your dialogue line.

850
00:37:16.580 --> 00:37:20.640
And sometimes that's hard to calibrate because you just start to feel it when you feel it.

851
00:37:21.060 --> 00:37:23.740
But I do remember this scene.

852
00:37:23.740 --> 00:37:24.940
I was so emotional.

853
00:37:25.200 --> 00:37:28.560
I don't know how many takes we did, but I had to hold that for the whole time.

854
00:37:29.180 --> 00:37:29.360
Wow.

855
00:37:29.700 --> 00:37:41.700
Yeah, you know, this was one of our last kind of everybody bullpen scenes because we knew that in the next episode, Andy was off pursuing his dream, and we don't see him until,

856
00:37:41.700 --> 00:37:43.000
like, the very end.

857
00:37:44.760 --> 00:37:47.880
And so, yeah, it felt like, wow.

858
00:37:47.880 --> 00:37:51.560
It felt like people's story arcs were wrapping up.

859
00:37:51.760 --> 00:37:51.900
Yeah.

860
00:37:52.240 --> 00:37:55.100
And this scene was a very tangible moment of that.

861
00:37:55.320 --> 00:37:55.560
Yes.

862
00:37:55.840 --> 00:38:00.180
In this scene of all the emotion, I do have one moment that I'm calling busted.

863
00:38:00.700 --> 00:38:01.200
What's that?

864
00:38:01.200 --> 00:38:11.540
At 15 minutes and 18 seconds, as Clark comes out of the kitchen into the bullpen, you can see Clark Duke for one second look right down the barrel of the camera.

865
00:38:11.800 --> 00:38:12.280
Oh, really?

866
00:38:12.780 --> 00:38:13.940
Just for a second.

867
00:38:14.340 --> 00:38:16.200
And we weren't supposed to do that.

868
00:38:16.300 --> 00:38:19.880
You know, we were not supposed to look right into the camera unless we had a talking head.

869
00:38:19.880 --> 00:38:22.120
Or unless there was, like, a scripted note.

870
00:38:22.380 --> 00:38:22.580
Exactly.

871
00:38:22.740 --> 00:38:22.860
Right.

872
00:38:23.060 --> 00:38:24.420
The way Jim would do that.

873
00:38:24.440 --> 00:38:24.660
Sure.

874
00:38:24.880 --> 00:38:25.100
Mm-hmm.

875
00:38:25.700 --> 00:38:30.700
Well, I had these guys pull an audio clip of the song, but I honestly don't even think I can listen to it.

876
00:38:30.920 --> 00:38:32.100
Oh, no, we need to.

877
00:38:32.100 --> 00:38:32.900
It's so emotional.

878
00:38:33.160 --> 00:38:34.600
I know, but we need to.

879
00:38:34.700 --> 00:38:37.100
We need to all – we've all been on this rewatch together.

880
00:38:37.300 --> 00:38:43.420
Everyone listening is here with us, and we're going to have to say goodbye to the show again, Jenna.

881
00:38:43.800 --> 00:38:44.340
We are.

882
00:38:44.600 --> 00:38:46.200
I don't mean – now you're tearing up.

883
00:38:46.340 --> 00:38:48.020
I don't want to make you sad, but –

884
00:38:48.020 --> 00:38:48.320
Okay.

885
00:38:48.320 --> 00:38:50.560
We are going – we can listen to it.

886
00:38:50.720 --> 00:38:50.980
Okay.

887
00:38:51.340 --> 00:38:51.560
Okay.

888
00:38:51.840 --> 00:38:53.000
We'll listen to it.

889
00:38:53.080 --> 00:38:53.720
Let me get some tissues.

890
00:38:54.100 --> 00:38:54.980
Here it is.

891
00:38:55.360 --> 00:38:58.120
Tuna, I'm a performer, and perform I shall.

892
00:39:07.470 --> 00:39:39.130
I wish – don't let your life pass that we had.

893
00:39:39.910 --> 00:39:45.080
I let the things got bad.

894
00:39:46.000 --> 00:39:51.740
How clearly I first saw you smiling in the sun.

895
00:39:52.360 --> 00:39:55.140
I want to feel your warmth upon.

896
00:39:55.500 --> 00:40:01.420
I want to be the ones I will weep.

897
00:40:12.220 --> 00:40:16.510
Don't let your life pass.

898
00:40:24.590 --> 00:40:30.330
Don't let the past see you by.

899
00:40:32.350 --> 00:40:34.850
And weep not for you.

900
00:40:42.790 --> 00:40:43.910
You know what it is.

901
00:40:44.450 --> 00:41:01.770
It's like I can't believe that we have a recording of like Ed singing to us, which is something that him and Creed and Craig and Kate, you know.

902
00:41:01.770 --> 00:41:04.550
So they would do when we were just hanging out.

903
00:41:04.730 --> 00:41:04.910
Yeah.

904
00:41:05.070 --> 00:41:05.230
Yeah.

905
00:41:05.230 --> 00:41:13.530
And so that song brings up all the memories of us hanging out, and it's like this is one of the crossover ones.

906
00:41:13.770 --> 00:41:18.010
This is like it was for the show, but it was also for us.

907
00:41:18.150 --> 00:41:18.530
Mm-hmm.

908
00:41:18.530 --> 00:41:20.570
And it just hits deep.

909
00:41:21.330 --> 00:41:21.490
Yeah.

910
00:41:22.170 --> 00:41:22.650
Mm-hmm.

911
00:41:22.650 --> 00:41:24.290
And it makes me miss Ed.

912
00:41:24.650 --> 00:41:26.050
It makes me miss Ed.

913
00:41:26.210 --> 00:41:29.050
It makes me miss all of us in a room together like that.

914
00:41:29.210 --> 00:41:29.550
Yeah.

915
00:41:29.550 --> 00:41:32.230
Because it was so, so fun.

916
00:41:32.410 --> 00:41:34.030
And so special.

917
00:41:34.370 --> 00:41:34.630
Yeah.

918
00:41:34.950 --> 00:41:43.350
And I think, you know, Andy's going to have his line about how you wish you were in the good times, you know, whatever that line is later.

919
00:41:43.630 --> 00:41:45.210
But we actually did know.

920
00:41:45.450 --> 00:41:46.850
We actually did realize.

921
00:41:46.850 --> 00:41:53.390
So I feel like we were really present to the specialness and also the limited time of this.

922
00:41:53.770 --> 00:41:56.730
Like we were aware it was coming to an end.

923
00:41:57.050 --> 00:41:59.530
So we were especially, it was heightened.

924
00:42:00.350 --> 00:42:00.530
Yeah.

925
00:42:01.910 --> 00:42:06.150
Well, you know, Phyllis and Stanley are going to have a talking head.

926
00:42:06.330 --> 00:42:08.210
They're facing out as well.

927
00:42:08.370 --> 00:42:08.910
Are they?

928
00:42:09.130 --> 00:42:09.330
Yep.

929
00:42:10.150 --> 00:42:12.610
They're going to say maybe Andy can make it.

930
00:42:12.930 --> 00:42:13.110
Yeah.

931
00:42:13.310 --> 00:42:15.010
They were so impressed by his song.

932
00:42:16.410 --> 00:42:19.970
And Phyllis says worse people make it all the time like Lil' Romeo.

933
00:42:20.390 --> 00:42:23.310
And Stanley is like, no, Lil' Romeo was good.

934
00:42:23.550 --> 00:42:29.370
I want you to know this scene was longer and the two of them debated musicians and artists for a bit.

935
00:42:29.450 --> 00:42:30.630
And it is so funny.

936
00:42:31.010 --> 00:42:34.050
It's not in deleted scenes, but it was in the shooting draft.

937
00:42:34.270 --> 00:42:42.030
I love Phyllis's reaction to Stanley saying that Lil' Romeo was good because it's like she's going to bite her tongue.

938
00:42:42.170 --> 00:42:44.330
Like I can't have this argument again.

939
00:42:44.330 --> 00:42:45.790
They've had it so many times.

940
00:42:45.870 --> 00:42:51.030
There's such a moment of assumed history between these two people in that moment.

941
00:42:51.750 --> 00:42:56.890
Well, I thought I was done crying as I was watching this episode, but no.

942
00:42:57.310 --> 00:43:02.210
Now we're going to go to Angela's desk and she's looking at tents on her computer.

943
00:43:02.770 --> 00:43:09.530
And Oscar's going to approach her, realize that she is looking at tents because she has nowhere else to be.

944
00:43:10.530 --> 00:43:11.850
What is wrong with me?

945
00:43:12.050 --> 00:43:13.810
And you know what?

946
00:43:13.910 --> 00:43:15.410
I'm going to read these letters.

947
00:43:15.770 --> 00:43:16.210
Okay.

948
00:43:16.290 --> 00:43:19.070
We got a lot of letters about this scene and they deserve to be read.

949
00:43:19.230 --> 00:43:19.530
Okay.

950
00:43:19.770 --> 00:43:20.350
Here it is.

951
00:43:20.850 --> 00:43:21.510
Susan C.

952
00:43:21.590 --> 00:43:22.330
in Plano, Texas.

953
00:43:22.330 --> 00:43:26.790
I have been waiting to write to you since this podcast began over four years ago.

954
00:43:27.230 --> 00:43:28.150
Now's the time.

955
00:43:28.550 --> 00:43:33.950
I would like you to know that the scene between Angela and Oscar, when Oscar sees Angela in distress,

956
00:43:34.330 --> 00:43:40.550
offers her living space until she gets on her feet and reaches over to place a comforting hand over hers.

957
00:43:40.890 --> 00:43:41.870
Oh, my gosh.

958
00:43:41.870 --> 00:43:46.450
This is the embodiment to me of grace and mercy.

959
00:43:47.050 --> 00:43:58.590
And after all they have been through together, all the ways they have wounded or tried to kneecap each other, all the ways they have irritated the fool out of one another,

960
00:43:58.990 --> 00:44:08.130
Oscar compassionately reaches out to his friend in love and she responds not with pride or rebuff, but with tender acceptance.

961
00:44:08.130 --> 00:44:14.670
I love this moment in the series so very much and commend both Angela and Oscar for their acting.

962
00:44:15.110 --> 00:44:18.750
It could have been maudlin, but instead it is pure gold.

963
00:44:18.910 --> 00:44:20.690
And I couldn't have said it better, Susan.

964
00:44:20.890 --> 00:44:21.290
Thank you.

965
00:44:21.910 --> 00:44:23.630
And Angela, Christine C.

966
00:44:23.830 --> 00:44:24.790
from New York said,

967
00:44:24.970 --> 00:44:31.670
One of my all-time favorite scenes is when Oscar tells Angela to come live with him and Angela takes his hand saying thank you.

968
00:44:31.910 --> 00:44:37.870
I've watched the show over a hundred times, no exaggeration, and this moment always moves me to tears.

969
00:44:38.130 --> 00:44:44.770
Angela, what was it like to approach this change in your character while also staying true to who she was?

970
00:44:45.490 --> 00:44:47.030
Oh, y'all are going to make me cry.

971
00:44:48.270 --> 00:44:51.610
You know, I approached it as...

972
00:44:51.610 --> 00:44:52.510
Oh, gosh.

973
00:44:52.850 --> 00:44:54.550
Are we going to make it to the finale?

974
00:44:54.550 --> 00:44:55.130
I don't know.

975
00:44:55.130 --> 00:44:56.630
Angela, we are a mess.

976
00:44:56.630 --> 00:44:57.570
We are a mess.

977
00:44:58.830 --> 00:45:04.510
You know, to play these characters, honestly, they had to be real people to us.

978
00:45:05.050 --> 00:45:09.790
And Angela's best friend in the office was always Oscar.

979
00:45:11.190 --> 00:45:18.510
Even though we kind of like that sibling that you love but can get under your skin more than anyone else.

980
00:45:18.630 --> 00:45:24.950
That familiarity breeds contempt person in your life, but is the only person you probably really truSt.

981
00:45:25.510 --> 00:45:26.010
Yeah.

982
00:45:26.010 --> 00:45:28.750
And that's how I played that relationship.

983
00:45:28.790 --> 00:45:33.530
Even though we had big disagreements, that he was my best friend.

984
00:45:34.310 --> 00:45:47.210
And so when he was so gracious and kind to me in that moment, I feel like all this pride that Angela had held on to had broken apart.

985
00:45:48.010 --> 00:45:51.450
And that's why she had that conversation with Andy in the parking lot.

986
00:45:51.690 --> 00:45:53.370
She was like, don't let pride get in the way.

987
00:45:54.150 --> 00:45:57.390
So thank you for noticing that in our performances.

988
00:45:58.030 --> 00:45:59.810
I'm really proud of that scene.

989
00:46:00.210 --> 00:46:04.550
And I'm really thankful I got to do it with Oscar, someone who I'd known for so long.

990
00:46:04.690 --> 00:46:09.150
And I trusted in real life so that I could go to that vulnerable place.

991
00:46:09.510 --> 00:46:14.590
But I want you guys to know one of the things I absolutely love when I rewatched this.

992
00:46:14.590 --> 00:46:16.930
I loved when I touch his hand.

993
00:46:17.190 --> 00:46:17.670
Same.

994
00:46:17.910 --> 00:46:19.590
That was what got me.

995
00:46:19.990 --> 00:46:20.270
Yeah.

996
00:46:20.450 --> 00:46:23.690
And I just said thank you to him from the bottom of my heart.

997
00:46:23.850 --> 00:46:24.030
Yep.

998
00:46:24.390 --> 00:46:33.410
But what I loved about doing scenes with Oscar is we could play this emotion and stay in it and then also find a comedic moment.

999
00:46:33.590 --> 00:46:35.890
When you ask him if his place allows pets.

1000
00:46:36.170 --> 00:46:37.690
I improvised that line.

1001
00:46:37.890 --> 00:46:38.730
Oh, lady.

1002
00:46:38.890 --> 00:46:39.810
And his response.

1003
00:46:40.110 --> 00:46:40.990
Oh, Angela.

1004
00:46:41.650 --> 00:46:43.230
That was not scripted.

1005
00:46:43.230 --> 00:46:47.230
The scene ended with, let's go get Phillip and we'll get your stuff.

1006
00:46:47.350 --> 00:46:47.530
Yeah.

1007
00:46:47.530 --> 00:46:48.250
And I say, okay.

1008
00:46:48.890 --> 00:46:50.290
That's where the scene ended.

1009
00:46:50.550 --> 00:46:52.650
And then we were to get up and walk out.

1010
00:46:52.830 --> 00:46:55.350
And Oscar and I had been in accounting for a long time.

1011
00:46:55.570 --> 00:47:00.590
We knew if we made it quick, especially on an exit, an improvised line might make it in.

1012
00:47:01.210 --> 00:47:03.050
So we didn't even talk about it.

1013
00:47:03.190 --> 00:47:05.290
He said, let's get you the hell out of that place.

1014
00:47:05.570 --> 00:47:07.490
And then there was this brief pause.

1015
00:47:07.490 --> 00:47:09.910
And I said, are you allowed to have pets?

1016
00:47:09.910 --> 00:47:11.810
And he's like, oh, Angela.

1017
00:47:12.010 --> 00:47:13.270
And it made it in.

1018
00:47:13.330 --> 00:47:15.610
And that delights me every time I see it.

1019
00:47:15.770 --> 00:47:22.290
Well, it's so great because it helps you release some of your emotion with a laugh at the end.

1020
00:47:22.510 --> 00:47:22.670
Yeah.

1021
00:47:22.910 --> 00:47:24.110
Oh, I love that moment.

1022
00:47:24.450 --> 00:47:26.210
I did not know that was improvised.

1023
00:47:26.210 --> 00:47:28.270
Oh, so good.

1024
00:47:28.630 --> 00:47:30.270
Dwight now has a talking head.

1025
00:47:30.410 --> 00:47:35.730
He says just yesterday he was a paper salesman with a farm and a dream about beet fuel.

1026
00:47:35.870 --> 00:47:38.610
But today he's regional manager with a black belt.

1027
00:47:38.870 --> 00:47:41.890
It's amazing how life can change in one day.

1028
00:47:42.070 --> 00:47:45.770
I'd like to point out that his talking head is facing towards the bullpen.

1029
00:47:45.930 --> 00:47:48.490
Because his future is at Dunder Mifflin.

1030
00:47:48.570 --> 00:47:48.870
Yeah.

1031
00:47:48.870 --> 00:47:51.170
I love that so much.

1032
00:47:51.810 --> 00:48:02.490
Well, speaking about futures, Daryl is going to find Jim in the kitchen and share some happy news that Athlete received an offer for a buyout.

1033
00:48:03.090 --> 00:48:06.650
And they want them to go on the road for three months.

1034
00:48:06.650 --> 00:48:10.510
They want them to pitch out west because they don't want this to be a regional thing.

1035
00:48:10.510 --> 00:48:12.310
They want Athlete to be national.

1036
00:48:13.370 --> 00:48:16.030
And Daryl's like, we're going on the road, buddy.

1037
00:48:16.030 --> 00:48:16.990
We did it.

1038
00:48:17.170 --> 00:48:18.530
He's so excited.

1039
00:48:18.870 --> 00:48:21.130
But Jim says, I can't do it.

1040
00:48:21.910 --> 00:48:23.330
I can't do it to Pam.

1041
00:48:23.970 --> 00:48:25.910
And Daryl's like, can't believe it.

1042
00:48:26.710 --> 00:48:31.530
And they kind of walk out and you see that Pam has overheard this from the bathroom.

1043
00:48:32.310 --> 00:48:33.890
Which I think is so important.

1044
00:48:34.650 --> 00:48:36.410
I'm so glad they had that moment.

1045
00:48:37.150 --> 00:48:38.050
I am too.

1046
00:48:38.430 --> 00:48:40.110
And I know where this is going.

1047
00:48:40.250 --> 00:48:43.030
And I have a few gripes about it.

1048
00:48:43.110 --> 00:48:45.550
But I'll bring them up next week when we get to them.

1049
00:48:46.190 --> 00:48:46.630
Okay.

1050
00:48:46.950 --> 00:48:47.310
Hold it.

1051
00:48:47.390 --> 00:48:47.670
Hold it.

1052
00:48:47.710 --> 00:48:48.150
I will.

1053
00:48:48.150 --> 00:48:52.790
Now we have this scene of Angela and Oscar in Oscar's car.

1054
00:48:52.950 --> 00:48:54.050
They're in the parking lot.

1055
00:48:54.690 --> 00:48:57.350
And Angela starts it off kind of snarky.

1056
00:48:57.530 --> 00:49:00.550
She's like, so is your place all bachelor, slobby, and gross?

1057
00:49:00.850 --> 00:49:03.250
And Oscar's like, no, it's neat and tasteful.

1058
00:49:03.250 --> 00:49:06.030
Yes, you said it really lives up to the gay stereotype.

1059
00:49:06.630 --> 00:49:06.810
Yeah.

1060
00:49:07.170 --> 00:49:14.450
And then Angela, oh, the sass still in her, even when she's at her broken lowest moment.

1061
00:49:14.450 --> 00:49:15.730
She goes, I wouldn't know.

1062
00:49:15.910 --> 00:49:17.190
I never lived with a gay guy.

1063
00:49:17.510 --> 00:49:20.030
And Oscar's like, Angela, you were juSt.

1064
00:49:20.290 --> 00:49:20.750
Yeah.

1065
00:49:21.430 --> 00:49:22.390
He's like, you did.

1066
00:49:22.530 --> 00:49:22.970
You did.

1067
00:49:22.970 --> 00:49:28.270
And then she completely breaks down and starts sobbing.

1068
00:49:28.650 --> 00:49:30.550
And she says, I love him.

1069
00:49:30.770 --> 00:49:33.470
And Oscar thinks she's talking about the senator.

1070
00:49:33.470 --> 00:49:36.190
And she says, no, I love Dwight.

1071
00:49:36.190 --> 00:49:39.610
Now, Angela, I know you've shared this before in different places.

1072
00:49:39.610 --> 00:49:42.670
But will you tell people how you got to this cry?

1073
00:49:43.010 --> 00:49:48.030
There was this moment, a piece of direction from Jeff Blitz that really helped you here.

1074
00:49:48.030 --> 00:49:51.910
Well, in the other scenes, my cry could build.

1075
00:49:52.510 --> 00:49:56.390
But in this scene, they wanted me to all of a sudden break down.

1076
00:49:56.950 --> 00:50:00.450
They wanted just her to break apart.

1077
00:50:00.970 --> 00:50:03.430
And that's harder to do.

1078
00:50:03.830 --> 00:50:10.850
Because emotionally, you can, like when Andy was playing the guitar, there were so many moments I could run through my mind to be teary.

1079
00:50:11.270 --> 00:50:15.770
But this had to go from kind of being snarky to an instant breakdown.

1080
00:50:16.050 --> 00:50:16.230
Yeah.

1081
00:50:16.230 --> 00:50:19.650
So we did one take, and I did break down.

1082
00:50:19.930 --> 00:50:21.990
I kind of built up to it a little bit.

1083
00:50:22.810 --> 00:50:27.250
And then Jeff came over to me and said, Angela, that was great.

1084
00:50:27.250 --> 00:50:28.470
And now I have that.

1085
00:50:29.090 --> 00:50:31.230
And he said, can you step out of the car for a second?

1086
00:50:31.230 --> 00:50:32.090
I want to talk to you.

1087
00:50:32.390 --> 00:50:33.090
I said, OK.

1088
00:50:33.710 --> 00:50:35.170
So Oscar stayed in the car.

1089
00:50:35.190 --> 00:50:37.710
And he said, will you do a favor for me?

1090
00:50:37.870 --> 00:50:38.810
And I said, yeah.

1091
00:50:38.950 --> 00:50:41.250
And he said, oh, it's going to make me cry.

1092
00:50:41.570 --> 00:50:42.610
That's a good direction.

1093
00:50:42.610 --> 00:50:47.290
He said, in this take, will you say goodbye to the show?

1094
00:50:48.010 --> 00:50:51.670
And will you say goodbye to all the characters?

1095
00:50:51.950 --> 00:50:54.570
And will you say goodbye to playing Angela Martin?

1096
00:50:54.570 --> 00:51:00.950
So on your line, I love him, the subtext he wanted was goodbye.

1097
00:51:01.250 --> 00:51:04.190
Goodbye to these people I love.

1098
00:51:04.390 --> 00:51:04.730
Mm-hmm.

1099
00:51:05.350 --> 00:51:06.590
And this character.

1100
00:51:07.170 --> 00:51:12.930
And so I was thinking about that, even as I said my snarky lines.

1101
00:51:13.210 --> 00:51:13.590
Mm-hmm.

1102
00:51:13.590 --> 00:51:19.490
And so when I got to I Love Him, it was, I'm never going to get to do this again.

1103
00:51:19.990 --> 00:51:20.470
Yeah.

1104
00:51:20.710 --> 00:51:22.650
This is it for me on this show.

1105
00:51:23.530 --> 00:51:26.950
Nine years of my life, I'm saying goodbye to.

1106
00:51:27.130 --> 00:51:30.830
And I cried, big, ugly cry.

1107
00:51:31.090 --> 00:51:37.990
I cried so hard that after the take, Jeff came up to me and said, that was fantastic.

1108
00:51:38.730 --> 00:51:39.970
I can't use it.

1109
00:51:40.070 --> 00:51:40.830
It's too much.

1110
00:51:41.070 --> 00:51:42.470
That's what happened to me.

1111
00:51:42.470 --> 00:51:46.910
Right when Paul Feig told me to say goodbye to Steve at the airport.

1112
00:51:47.150 --> 00:51:47.730
Oh, my gosh.

1113
00:51:47.910 --> 00:51:49.430
It was like, that was great.

1114
00:51:49.610 --> 00:51:50.950
And he said, I don't want to say too much.

1115
00:51:51.030 --> 00:51:52.330
He said, I want you to stay in it.

1116
00:51:52.470 --> 00:51:54.850
Can you do that just a little less?

1117
00:51:55.330 --> 00:51:58.850
And you guys, some people, I guess they can cry and look attractive.

1118
00:51:58.850 --> 00:51:59.550
Not me.

1119
00:51:59.750 --> 00:52:03.030
When I cry, it is like a full body wheezing.

1120
00:52:03.030 --> 00:52:04.330
I can't talk.

1121
00:52:05.710 --> 00:52:07.970
But what you see is real tears.

1122
00:52:07.970 --> 00:52:10.590
And it's me saying goodbye to the show in that moment.

1123
00:52:10.590 --> 00:52:15.170
And I wanted to share one thing that just delighted me.

1124
00:52:15.170 --> 00:52:19.710
I found an article that the AV Club did about this episode.

1125
00:52:20.150 --> 00:52:20.290
Oh.

1126
00:52:20.550 --> 00:52:22.330
It was written by Joshua Alston.

1127
00:52:22.610 --> 00:52:29.290
And he was very excited to finally get to review an episode of season nine in particular because he was a big fan of season nine.

1128
00:52:29.290 --> 00:52:34.730
And the first one he was assigned to do was living the dream.

1129
00:52:34.950 --> 00:52:36.750
And it wasn't his favorite.

1130
00:52:37.110 --> 00:52:37.950
Oh, no.

1131
00:52:37.950 --> 00:52:40.130
But he wrote this.

1132
00:52:40.390 --> 00:52:47.210
I can't help but wonder if I'd have the same impression of living the dream if I hadn't read that it was originally planned as a half hour installment,

1133
00:52:47.210 --> 00:52:49.370
then padded out to fill an hour.

1134
00:52:49.570 --> 00:52:50.950
But I suspect I would.

1135
00:52:51.150 --> 00:52:52.570
I hope this gets better.

1136
00:52:53.030 --> 00:52:59.910
And he goes on to point out some of the things he liked about it, but that it had just kind of been stretched out maybe more than it needed to be.

1137
00:53:00.110 --> 00:53:01.410
Listen, I felt that.

1138
00:53:01.590 --> 00:53:01.910
Yes.

1139
00:53:01.910 --> 00:53:09.450
I felt that, but I also know that the things that hit in this episode, they couldn't have been done in 22 minutes.

1140
00:53:09.470 --> 00:53:14.390
So sorry if you had to sit through a couple of repetitive beats, but it's what needed to be.

1141
00:53:14.670 --> 00:53:14.970
Yes.

1142
00:53:15.130 --> 00:53:18.350
And then at the end of his review, he said this.

1143
00:53:18.590 --> 00:53:25.950
I didn't talk about the Angela story because I didn't want to go into too much detail, but her life sucks now that she's left the state senator.

1144
00:53:25.950 --> 00:53:32.910
Her cats were seized, she got evicted from her apartment, and is apparently a double-digit bank transfer away from indigents.

1145
00:53:33.150 --> 00:53:40.330
I'd love for Dwight and Angela to end up together, but I wish the writers had chosen a path that didn't involve Angela being reduced to nothing firSt.

1146
00:53:40.670 --> 00:53:48.990
That said, an uptight gay Mexican sharing an apartment with the differently uptight school marm whose ex-husband is his former lover?

1147
00:53:48.990 --> 00:53:49.850
Question mark?

1148
00:53:50.190 --> 00:53:57.010
The words, the office spinoff usually make me break out, but in all caps, that is a show I would watch.

1149
00:53:57.250 --> 00:53:57.550
Yeah.

1150
00:54:00.050 --> 00:54:01.630
I always felt that way too.

1151
00:54:01.790 --> 00:54:04.330
I was like, Angela and Oscar sharing an apartment?

1152
00:54:04.890 --> 00:54:05.590
Sign me up.

1153
00:54:05.690 --> 00:54:06.690
It's like the odd couple.

1154
00:54:06.950 --> 00:54:09.170
I wish we could see more of that.

1155
00:54:09.410 --> 00:54:09.590
Yeah.

1156
00:54:09.930 --> 00:54:16.750
Well, I'll have you know that critically, this episode was very well received.

1157
00:54:16.750 --> 00:54:27.150
And in fact, these last six episodes, Live in the Dream Part 1, Live in the Dream Part 2, AARM Part 1, AARM Part 2, Finale 1 and 2,

1158
00:54:27.770 --> 00:54:34.350
this block of six episodes were rated the highest among office tally.com viewers as well.

1159
00:54:34.770 --> 00:54:41.250
There is this stretch here where we got people excited, like the critics and fans alike.

1160
00:54:41.290 --> 00:54:43.090
They liked where this was going.

1161
00:54:43.690 --> 00:54:49.570
Well, by this time, we're all so invested in these characters and big life stuff starts happening.

1162
00:54:51.230 --> 00:54:53.110
Well, that's the end of this episode.

1163
00:54:53.270 --> 00:54:56.510
Thank you, Steve Burgess, for all of your behind-the-scenes tidbits.

1164
00:54:56.710 --> 00:54:58.330
And thank you all for writing in.

1165
00:54:58.710 --> 00:55:00.770
And Angela, thank you for your nifty gifties.

1166
00:55:00.950 --> 00:55:01.830
You're welcome.

1167
00:55:02.170 --> 00:55:03.450
And thank you, Mary.

1168
00:55:04.110 --> 00:55:04.570
Beatrice.

1169
00:55:04.870 --> 00:55:05.730
Davidson-Kinner.

1170
00:55:05.730 --> 00:55:11.990
Yes, for inventing the toilet paper roll hook and sanitary napkin.

1171
00:55:12.210 --> 00:55:18.950
When she did the sanitary belt specifically, she did it with her sister, Mildred Davidson-Austin Smith.

1172
00:55:19.390 --> 00:55:20.410
So it was two sisters.

1173
00:55:20.410 --> 00:55:22.910
Two sisters helping ladies out.

1174
00:55:23.110 --> 00:55:24.150
I mean, amazing.

1175
00:55:24.350 --> 00:55:24.730
Amazing.

1176
00:55:25.270 --> 00:55:26.150
Well, there you go.

1177
00:55:26.310 --> 00:55:27.950
That's Living the Dream Part 2, everybody.

1178
00:55:28.270 --> 00:55:29.050
Thank you for listening.

1179
00:55:29.270 --> 00:55:30.450
We love doing this.

1180
00:55:30.530 --> 00:55:31.870
And we hope you have a great day.

1181
00:55:32.170 --> 00:55:33.050
We'll see you next week.

1182
00:55:33.050 --> 00:55:39.390
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.

